    ('76cd8b60-c373-4f26-85ac-2827b0797b15'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Ahmose founded a new age for a unified land, ruled from this city. On the Nile''s east bank stand the temples of Karnak and Luxor; royal cemeteries spread over the west bank.', 'Within modern Luxor lie the ruins of Thebes, inhabited from around 3200 BC: the temples of Karnak and Luxor on the Nile''s eastern bank, royal cemeteries on its western bank.', 'teaser-card-s036-rollback:76cd8b60-c373-4f26-85ac-2827b0797b15:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s036: card_description "Within modern Luxor lie the ruins of Thebes, inhabited from around 3200 BC: the temples of Karnak and Luxor on the Nile''s eastern bank, royal cemeteries on its western bank." restored on Thebes', 'ee7d429161beb955b16989056ce9ac7ef5834f58783125d3b9ddce2acbeae2a0|161e880d372475a7f974c7b188e2139ac983d939ffb1f0d8aeb71f2663529d8b|161e880d372475a7f974c7b188e2139ac983d939ffb1f0d8aeb71f2663529d8b', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite1-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ahmose founded a new age for a unified land, ruled from this city. On the Nile''s east bank stand the temples of Karnak and Luxor; royal cemeteries spread over the west bank."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check1-002 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ahmose founded a new age [S6]; that age was one of a unified land [S6]; the land was ruled from this city (it was the capital) [S6]; the temples of Karnak and Luxor stand on the Nile''s east bank [S4]; royal cemeteries lie on the west bank [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-004 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ahmose founded a new age, from this city. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmose_I]; The new age Ahmose founded was one of a unified land. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmose_I]; The unified land was ruled from this city. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmose_I]; The temple of Karnak stands on the Nile''s east bank. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luxor_Temple]; The temple of Luxor stands on the Nile''s east bank. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luxor_Temple]; Royal cemeteries spread over the west bank. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_of_the_Kings]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('817ff7b7-a814-405a-a5af-0ef173f07045'::uuid, 'card_description', 'A Baroque triumphal arch replaced the eastern tower of this Roman bridge in 1721. The western tower dates from a rebuild after a flood and bears the arms of the Catholic Monarchs.', 'Below the Castillo de San Servando, the Roman Puente de Alcántara spans the Tagus in Toledo. Its name comes from the Arabic for arch; in 1721 a Baroque arch replaced its eastern tower.', 'teaser-card-s036-rollback:817ff7b7-a814-405a-a5af-0ef173f07045:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s036: card_description ''Below the Castillo de San Servando, the Roman Puente de Alcántara spans the Tagus in Toledo. Its name comes from the Arabic for arch; in 1721 a Baroque arch replaced its eastern tower.'' restored on Puente de Alcántara', 'f0ef0048306940e9e65fd0278a83b681a448bdc59ebdad5d2f903b36948fc495|479d7ccf5d0663dbded51bff67a6a911e2619226d8abd1746a5281a191692b51|479d7ccf5d0663dbded51bff67a6a911e2619226d8abd1746a5281a191692b51', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite-v-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A Baroque triumphal arch replaced the eastern tower of this Roman bridge in 1721. The western tower dates from a rebuild after a flood and bears the arms of the Catholic Monarchs."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-v-001 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "a Baroque triumphal arch replaced the eastern tower [S6]; the replacement happened in 1721 [S6]; the site is a Roman bridge [S1]; the bridge was damaged by a flood and rebuilt [S4]; the western tower dates from that rebuild [S5]; the western tower bears the arms of the Catholic Monarchs [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify2-002 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A triumphal arch replaced the eastern tower of this bridge in 1721. [SUPPORTED: https://cultura.castillalamancha.es/patrimonio/catalogo-patrimonio-cultural/puente-de-alcantara-de-toledo]; The triumphal arch that replaced the eastern tower is Baroque. [SUPPORTED: https://www.turismocastillalamancha.es/es/cultura-y-patrimonio/monumentos/toledo/puente-de-alcantara-(toledo)]; This is a Roman bridge. [SUPPORTED: https://cultura.castillalamancha.es/patrimonio/catalogo-patrimonio-cultural/puente-de-alcantara-de-toledo]; The western tower dates from a rebuild. [SUPPORTED: https://cultura.castillalamancha.es/patrimonio/catalogo-patrimonio-cultural/puente-de-alcantara-de-toledo]; That rebuild came after a flood. [SUPPORTED: https://www.eldiario.es/viajes/levantado-siglo-iii-puente-tuvo-origen-torreones-primeros-construyeron-tajo-pm_1_12981888.html]; The western tower bears the arms of the Catholic Monarchs. [SUPPORTED: https://cultura.castillalamancha.es/patrimonio/catalogo-patrimonio-cultural/puente-de-alcantara-de-toledo]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('a3a38d98-16fc-464f-bbeb-c027813ef202'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Sculptures of Jupiter Dolichenus have been found in this ancient Roman settlement. In the 3rd century BC, the area was inhabited by a people called the Scordisci.', 'Celtic Scordisci lived in this area in the 3rd century BC. Here lay Acumincum, a Roman settlement in the town of Stari Slankamen, where sculptures of Jupiter Dolichenus have been found.', 'teaser-card-s036-rollback:a3a38d98-16fc-464f-bbeb-c027813ef202:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s036: card_description ''Celtic Scordisci lived in this area in the 3rd century BC. Here lay Acumincum, a Roman settlement in the town of Stari Slankamen, where sculptures of Jupiter Dolichenus have been found.'' restored on Acumincum', '306b8e06556e4941b1407adc5532d55e1982ff44b7b3c8caca3d9ad2258b791f|6f17a3440b4a583f4abca3b12b3012bc182ba03964e78f99b5d5e7f29bb211e5|6f17a3440b4a583f4abca3b12b3012bc182ba03964e78f99b5d5e7f29bb211e5', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite-v-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Sculptures of Jupiter Dolichenus have been found in this ancient Roman settlement. In the 3rd century BC, the area was inhabited by a people called the Scordisci."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "sculptures of Jupiter Dolichenus have been found at the site [S4]; the site is an ancient Roman settlement [S1]; in the 3rd century BC the area was inhabited by the Scordisci [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify2-002 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot3-2026-10-20/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Sculptures of Jupiter Dolichenus have been found in this ancient R